msgstr ""

#: htdocs/luci-static/resources/view/accesscontrol/overview.js:437
msgid ""
"Holiday mode dates each part of a period by the day it belongs to: a part "
"crossing midnight follows its end date, and a part from 18:00 on follows the "
"next day, so the night before a holiday stays open and the last holiday "
"night is restricted. A period that reaches 18:00 is split at that boundary. "
"For example 20:10–08:00 and 21:30–22:00 are both unrestricted on an ordinary "
"Friday night and restricted on the last holiday night, while 17:00–18:30 "
"keeps 17:00–18:00 on the current day and follows the next day from 18:00."
msgstr ""

#: htdocs/luci-static/resources/view/accesscontrol/overview.js:438
msgid ""
"Holiday mode follows the router's own timezone from System → Timezone for "
"both the period times and the holiday dates, so a China holiday calendar "
"needs the router set to a UTC+8 zone."
msgstr ""

#: htdocs/luci-static/resources/view/accesscontrol/overview.js:439
msgid ""
"Holiday mode includes the entire end minute: an end time of 06:00 remains "
"restricted through 06:00:59 and releases at 06:01. Equal start and end times "
"restrict only that minute."
msgstr ""

#: htdocs/luci-static/resources/view/accesscontrol/overview.js:440
msgid ""
"If calendar data is unavailable, this rule uses its selected weekdays. If "
"calendar rules cannot be applied, the previous rules remain in place while "
"the service retries."
msgstr ""

